{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-figure-eight-reeb-rotation","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:figure-eight-reeb-rotation","kind":"proposition","title":"The figure-eight knot operator acts unitarily on $V_{(2,1)}$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-hoefsmit-binding-amplitude","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-reeb-flow"],"cites":["references/jones1987","references/wenzl1988c","references/kashaev1997"],"tags":["figure-eight","4_1","reeb-flow","unitary","knot-operator","volume-conjecture","lepton-channel-rotation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figure_eight_unitary_on_standard","text":"figure-eight-reeb-rotation.md","leanSource":"figure-eight-reeb-rotation.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:figure-eight-reeb-rotation\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi = (1+\\sqrt5)/2</code>. For every real <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi^{-1} &#x3C; q &#x3C; \\varphi</code>, the figure-eight knot operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M_{4_1} = (\\sigma_1\\sigma_2^{-1})^2</code>, acting on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_{(2,1)}</code>, has eigenvalues of unit modulus:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\lambda_{4_1} = e^{\\pm i\\theta},\n  \\qquad |\\lambda_{4_1}| = 1.</code></pre>\n<p>Its reading as a <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Reeb rotation angle is given in <a href=\"figure-eight-reeb-rotation-reeb-reading.md\">rem:figure-eight-reeb-rotation-reeb-reading</a>.</p>\n<p>At the endpoints <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in \\{\\varphi^{-1}, \\varphi\\}</code> the eigenvalue is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>, and for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > \\varphi</code> or <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0 &#x3C; q &#x3C; \\varphi^{-1}</code> the eigenvalues are real and not of unit modulus.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/figure-eight-reeb-rotation.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"7.10.18","page":"b/prop-figure-eight-reeb-rotation","qa":{"counts":{"pass":89,"fail":2,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":75},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figure_eight_unitary_on_standard","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/figure-eight-reeb-rotation.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
